  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a SwiftHFR user, I want one system search entry and consistent haptic feedback across the app, so that the app feels like one native whole rather than screens built one by one.\n\n**M5** (operator decision 2026-11-09): an evolution, not legacy parity. Status `blocked` until M5 opens.\n\n### On hold\n\nHeld by the M5_OPEN decision: M5 opens after the M4 parity is validated, and the orchestrator opens it (operator decisions of 2026-11-02 on #379). ([decision](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379#issuecomment-6573879240))\n\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Unified search**: `.searchable` entry points (forum search, topic search, smiley search, filtered posts), placement per the iOS 27 HIG; today every search is its own screen.\n- **Haptics**: one small catalogue (selection, success, warning) applied consistently (tab re-select UXD-04 #426, swipe actions, send/confirm, errors) through `.sensoryFeedback`, respecting system settings.\n- **Phase 5 design documentation**: the maintainer's design document announced in ROADMAP Phase 5, which LOT-147 (#237, Duo and iPad columns) needs; this issue tracks its arrival.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A short spec (`docs/features/` or a lot spec) chooses the search and haptic patterns, with HIG sources.\n- [ ] The consistency matrix of the M4 issue gets the two columns filled for M5.\n- [ ] The Phase 5 design document is linked here, or its absence is recorded.\n\nRelated: #693, #545, #572, LOT-147 (#237).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
